    "claim": "When you sell crypto at a profit in a regular account, 50% of the gain is added to your taxable income. A $10,000 gain adds $5,000 to your income, and that $5,000 is taxed at your top rate. If your taxable income is between about $58,523 and $107,785 in 2026, that rate is 20.5% federal plus 9.15% Ontario, or 29.65%, which comes to about $1,483. At income under $53,891 the combined rate is 19.05% (about $953), and higher brackets owe more. Ontario surtax, the Ontario Health Premium and credits can shift the exact amount, and gains inside a TFSA are not taxed.",
